e that might be might not be  revealed rather in the weeks to come our  jackson proska reports on the latest in  a long list of legal woes facing trump  in a compromise meant to protect  sensitive information a florida judge  ordered the u.s government to redact  portions of the affidavit used in the  search of donald trump's mar-a-lago home  all for possible release  lawyers for the justice department  revealed their investigation is still in  its early stages it would certainly give  insight and reveal what the doj is  investigating how they know what they  know where they've been looking in court  filings justice officials warned  releasing the affidavit would serve as a  road map to the government's ongoing  investigation  doj lawyers say they're deeply concerned  about the safety of witnesses whose  participation led to the recovery of 11  sets of classified documents from  trump's home tell us the predicate for  the warrant reveal the affidavit this is  too important to democracy  but the former president and his allies  have insisted the underlying reasons for  the search warrant should be public  trump's lawyers notably did not  intervene to support the unsealing  but trump faces legal jeopardy on  multiple fronts federal prosecutors have  issued a grand jury subpoena for all of  the white house documents turned over to  the january 6th committee they're  investigating the role of trump and his  allies in the attack on the capitol  in new york alan weiselberg the former  chief financial officer at the trump  organization pleaded guilty to  conspiring with the company on a 15-year  tax fraud he'll spend five months in  prison in exchange for testifying at an  upcoming trial into the business  practices of trump's namesake company  and this week in georgia trump lawyer  rudy giuliani testified before a grand  jury part of a criminal investigation  into election interference in the state  i'm not going to comment on the grand  jury investigation the latest moves by  the court in florida suggest prosecution  is not necessarily imminent over the  mishandling of classified documents  but it's clear trump's legal troubles  are far from over  jackson prosko global news washington  almost four years after he was found  bludgeoned to death in his prison cell  charges have now been laid in the  killing of notorious gangster james  whitey bulger three men including a  mafia hit man have been indicted on  conspiracy to commit first degree murder  two of the accused were already behind  bars bulger was one of america's most  infamous mob bosses he was number two on  the fbi's most wanted list behind osama  bin laden before his arrest in 2011.  unprecedented sentence ahead why this  woman is being imprisoned for her social  media posts  [Music]  a bombing at a mosque in the afghan  capital of kabul has left at least 21  people dead and wounded more than 30  others heightened security can be seen  around the mosque one day after the  deadly blast ripped through the facility  during evening prayers no group has  claimed responsibility for the attack  but the islamic state has said it's  responsible for similar attacks carried  out in recent months there are fears the  death toll could rise as several of the  injured including children are still in  the hospital  a saudi court has sentenced a women's  rights advocate to 34 years in prison  for posting critical tweets and the  ruling is drawing outrage around the  world salma al-shahab was detained  during a family vacation last year just  days after she planned to return to the  united kingdom before the trip she  tweeted or retweeted several messages  calling for reforms in saudi arabia and  the release of activists a terrorism  tribunal convicted al-shahab of helping  dissidents and publishing false rumors  the unusually harsh sentence comes amid  crown prince mohammed bin salman's  crackdown on critics  three days of heavy rain has caused  major damage to roads and homes on new  zealand's south island  an atmospheric river has brought more  than 300 millimeters of rain in just the  past 24 hours several rivers have burst  their banks submerging roads and homes  and dozens of midslides have also come  down  so far more than 300 homes have been  evacuated and a severe weather warning  is still in place as another significant  rainfall is in the forecast  and at least six people are dead and at  least 20 people were hurt after a  powerful storm battered the french  mediterranean island of corsica heavy  rain and wind gusts topping 220  kilometers per hour swept across the  island uprooting trees and damaging  homes across the popular tourist  destination as many as 40 000 homes and  businesses are without power and more  rain is expected over the next 24 hours  a chaotic scene was caught on camera in  the peruvian capital of lima after a  bull slated for the slaughterhouse got  loose and caused a panic  the frightened animal sent people  running after escaping from the truck it  was being transported in the bull tore  through shops and reportedly injured at  least one person it was eventually  caught by locals in the area some 40  minutes after its capture  the meme that gained huge momentum next  the canadian behind a powerful new brand  in ukraine  it started as a meme a symbol that pairs  a traditional orthodox religious icon  with a high-tech tank-killing missile  now a canadian with ukrainian roots has  turned saint javelin into a brand and  high-profile figures including ukraine's  president have been spotted wearing the  armed figure as europe bureau chief  crystal gomensing reports saint javelin  is now hard at work raising both morale  and money for the ukrainian cause  a meme turned lifeline  somebody's there at the front for us and  we are here for them victoria redenko  and all the seamstresses working on the  saint javelin line  know their products help fund the  ukrainian armed forces to say it is a  labor of love  doesn't begin to scratch the surface  i have a son-in-law he's near donetsk  sometimes the illusion is created  everything is fine  and the work distract us because if we  were left with ourselves it would be  much harder  bassline is one of several ukrainian  businesses contracted to produce items  under the saint javelin brand  a former journalist in toronto with  ukrainian roots christian boris started  it with a borrowed image of the madonna  from a few stickers to a canadian  storefront st javelin has brought in  roughly 1.2 million dollars  in ukraine st javelin is now an icon of  the war a symbol of ukrainian resistance  one of the aim was to find  manufacturers that are in  areas  that need help that were  affected by the war if you can help your  help  this printing facility in nepro has  turned out about 1700 t-shirts  a big change from the days of filling  molotov cocktails on the production  floor  one of the project managers  is also a soldier  i think this is very cool and once again  i am convinced that the entire civilized  world has rallied around ukraine  a morale booster with a canadian  connection  being shipped around the world  crystal gavinson global news  keith  and that's it for global national for  this thursday night i'm farah nasser and  on behalf of our whole crew i want to  thank you so much for spending part of  your evening with us tonight's york  canada is this herd of dairy cows in  bybank saskatchewan we love seeing your  canada so please keep emailing us your  pictures to viewers at  globalnational.com  until tomorrow take care of yourselves  and each other good night  [Music]  you
 

